<title>TURKEY: Turkey sells one-year bonds at 109.02 percent.</title>
<headline>Turkey sells one-year bonds at 109.02 percent.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish Treasury's one-year bond auction produced the following results on Tuesday.</p>
<p>	Maturity		    : March 11, 1998</p>
<p>	Amount			: 217.7 trln lira</p>
<p>	Minimum yield	     : -</p>
<p>	Maximum yield	     : 109.02</p>
<p>	Average yield	     : -</p>
<p>	Bid amount/cover	  : 517.1 trln lira</p>
<p>	Lowest accepted price   : 47,842 lira</p>
<p>	Payment date		: March 11, 1997</p>
<p>Banks will pay 102 trillion lira to the Treasury for the auction on Wednesday when 106.9 trillion lira of bills will mature.</p>
<p>The Treasury had last sold a record 380.1 trillion lira of 287-day bills at 112.86 percent yield on February 25.</p>
<p>It launched inflation-indexed, two-year bonds last week, but sold only 18.6 trillion lira of them at 25 percent risk premium.</p>
<p>--Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
